{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310623,"nonce":"Nkk1eVpi1pBcKpLd99woX2WaGQI=","title":"Generic monomorphization gaps (untyped-ctor FIXED, generic-method-chain OPEN) + LLVM verify Twine-crash localization. Root of the ...","message":"The BalancedTree/TreeNode SIGILL (sttD, exit 132 `udf #0xc11f`) is **un-monomorphized generics → forward-ref trap stub**, NOT a stranded constructor (that was a separate earlier fix, 83bd13e6) and NOT the LLVM crash. Diagnosed 2026-06-22.\n\n**Mechanism.** A generic fn that reaches codegen still carrying `signature.type_params` is trap-stubbed at cranelift_backend.rs:713 (`!type_params.is_empty()` → `[trap-stub:generic]`). Callers of a stub cascade-trap (cranelift_backend.rs:738 `[trap-stub:cascade]`). The monomorphizer (ir/monomorphize.rs `extract_generic_call`) specializes a call only if it carries explicit `type_args` OR can infer them from a param typed `IrType::TypeVar(name)`. **Untyped Haxe params lower to `*void`, not TypeVar** → inference (lines 294-313) returns None → no specialization.\n\n**FIXED (commit \"fix(mono): specialize generic constructors...\"):** direct `new Foo\u003cInt,Int\u003e(...)` whose ctor has untyped params (e.g. `new(l,k,v,r,h=-1)`) lowered the ctor CallDirect with EMPTY type_args. Fix in hir_to_mir.rs New lowering (~18868): attach concrete type args (prefer explicit `\u003c...\u003e`, else class_type's GenericInstance/Class type_args; drop if any unresolved TypeVar) via `build_call_direct_with_type_args`. Repro shape = haxe.ds.TreeNode (self-ref `left`/`right` + `get_height()` called INSIDE the ctor — the in-ctor method-call is the trigger; 1 self-ref param works, 2 doesn't). Regression test compiler/tests/haxe/test_generic_ctor_untyped_selfref.hx (PASS). core_types_e2e + rayzor_stdlib_e2e + monomorph lib tests all green.\n\n**FIXED 2026-06-22 #2 (commit \"fix(mono): seed monomorphization of cross-module generic method chains\").** The full haxe.ds.BalancedTree chain (set→setLoop→balance→compare→new TreeNode\u003cK,V\u003e) now works cross-module, Int + String keys, bit-exact. KEY DISCOVERY (workflow wf_dae754c0 + experiments): the monomorphizer + its transitive propagation (propagate_transitive_fixups, monomorphize.rs:594 — an EXISTING worklist that cascades the whole chain via the caller's substitution map from ONE seed) were ALWAYS FINE. Proof: the SAME BalancedTree copied as a USER class IN-FILE works; copied to a SEPARATE FILE + imported it FAILS identically to stdlib. So it was never a monomorphizer/transitive gap — it was a **cross-module LOWERING gap**. Root: hir_to_mir method-call lowering (~12351) gates type_args attachment on `is_user_defined`; an imported method's entry call (`t.set(1,10)`) resolves to a cross-module fn that's NOT in the module at lowering (FunctionKind≠UserDefined, callee invisible → callee-based has_type_params=false) → fell to a no-type_args fallback → monomorphizer never SEEDED set\u003cInt,Int\u003e → whole chain stayed generic-stub. FIX: detect genericity from the **RECEIVER** (concrete Class/GenericInstance carrying type_args), not the invisible callee; route such calls through the type_args block and attach the receiver's type_args. Repro that finally cracked it: compare `[mcall] in[main]` lines same-file (present, [I32,I32]) vs cross-module (ABSENT). Diagnostics added (RAYZOR_DUMP_MONO `[mcall]`-style traces were temporary, removed). Regression test compiler/tests/haxe/test_balancedtree_crossmodule_mono.hx (PASS). 715 lib + 2 e2e green; Array/Map/String unaffected.\n\n**RESIDUAL LIMITATION (pre-existing, NOT introduced — my fix extends it to List):** stdlib iteration-protocol methods that lower to extern Imports (List.iterator, Map.keys → for-in) are unresolvable cross-module and cranelift `finalize_definitions` PANICS on the WHOLE module (\"can't resolve symbol iterator\", exit 101) — Map.keys already did this on baseline. I excluded `extern_functions` callees from the receiver-route, but List.iterator's extern isn't visible in the entry module at lowering, so List still hits it (132→101). The clean containment (trap-stub for unresolvable Import symbols) is blocked: cranelift's symbol_lookup_fn chain has dlsym added first/consulted-last, so any fallback I add preempts dlsym (risky); and an empty-body trap-stub at declare_function never fires (iterator is an extern, a different decl path at cranelift_backend.rs:3182). Left as-is; nue uses StringMap (hash)/Array, not List for-in.\n\n**LLVM Twine crash — LOCALIZED (commit \"fix(llvm): localize module verify...\"):** the reported nue crash (EXC_BAD_ACCESS `llvm::Twine::printOneChild`) was `module.verify()` BUILDING its error message for a function with a dangling operand. Fix: `verify_module_localized()` in llvm_jit_backend.rs sweeps each fn with `verify(false)` (plain bool, no message) to name offenders before the crashing module-level path. Now a named diagnostic, not a process crash. All 3 module.verify sites routed through it.\n\n**DIAGNOSTICS (the rayzor bin installs NO tracing subscriber, so warn!/debug! are silent — use these eprintln env gates):**\n- `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1` → `[trap-stub:generic]`, `[trap-stub:cascade]`, `[skip-stub:fwdref]`, `[safety-net:fwdref-stub]`, `[fn-ptr]` table, and now `[COMPILE_FAIL]` reason.\n- `RAYZOR_DUMP_MONO=1` → `[mono]` generic-call type_arg resolution / \"cannot infer type_param\" skips.\n- `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1` → per-module post-merge MIR (user module dumps last).\n\nExit 132 = SIGILL `udf #0xc11f` = a forward-ref/trap stub being called. lldb frame#1 = `TieredBackend::execute_function` calling the stub directly means the ENTRY fn (or main) is itself a cascade stub. See [[bugs_import_xmodule_member_resolution]], [[feedback_nue_drives_compiler_fixes]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_generic_monomorph_untyped_ctor` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}